## 3. Requirements Surgery

The system shall be user-friendly
  Problem: Extremely subjective and untestable. User-friendly has no clear technical meaning
  Clarification Question: What specific task should users complete, and what is an acceptable maximum time or error rate for a novice user
  Missing Information: The target user profile, specific tasks involved, and measurable usability thresholds
  Repaired Requirement: The system shall enable an authenticated student to complete a booking request in 3 or fewer screen interactions
The system shall notify users about bookings
  Problem: Unclear WHO gets notified, WHEN the notification triggers, WHAT triggers it, and HOW email, SMS, in-app
  Clarification Question: Which events require notifications, and what communication channel should be used
  Missing Information: Trigger conditions, notification channels, recipient roles, and message content requirements
  Repaired Requirement: The system shall send an automated email confirmation to the user within 60 seconds of a successful booking creation
The system shall allow staff to create, edit and delete bookings and send reminders
  Problem: Bundles multiple distinct capabilities into a single compound requirement ("mega-requirement"), making independent testing difficult.
  Clarification Question: Which specific staff roles are authorized to perform each action  and under what conditions can a booking be modified
  Missing Information: Role separation (Lecturer vs. Technician), state conditions for deletion/editing, and rules for automated reminders
  Repaired Requirement (Atomic):The system shall allow an authorized Technician to cancel an existing booking prior to the scheduled pick-up time



## 4. Functional Requirements

The system shall allow an authorized user to view equipment availability for a selected date range
The system shall prevent a user from completing a booking request if the selected equipment is already reserved for any part of that time slot
The system shall record the exact date, time, and user ID when equipment is checked out and returned by a technician



## 5. Quality Requirements

The system shall restrict equipment booking management and inventory modification features strictly to users authenticated with 'Technician' or 'Admin' role credentials. 
Protects inventory data from unauthorized changes or accidental deletion by standard users. 
Attempt to access administrative management endpoints using a standard 'Student' user account and verify access is denied (HTTP 403 Forbidden). 



